{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "0b93a312-da6c-816e-a469-d51b80929f4a",
  "created_at": "2026-01-02T10:58:38-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Linh Tran",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:54:29-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise. Happy new year, how can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:54:35-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Happy new year. Yeah, hi. Um, I'm calling about water at the curb that won't go anywhere. Linh Tran, I manage a building over on Kingston Avenue."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:54:47-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Ms. Tran. What's the address there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:54:51-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "179 Kingston Avenue. Historic Hill, up past the church, kind of near the corner."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:54:57-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And what's it doing, the water? Is there a storm drain there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:55:03-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a drain at the curb, yes. It's not taking anything. We've had no rain, nothing. It's the melt from the snowbank, and it just sits there in a big puddle along the curb. Then overnight it freezes. So every morning I've got a sheet of black ice out front."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:55:23-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, that's no good. How long has it been going on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:55:28-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Since before Christmas, off and on. It's not the first time I've mentioned it, to be honest, but nothing's changed. Every time it warms up a little, the puddle comes back and then it freezes again. I put salt down. The salt is doing its best."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:55:47-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. Is it in the street or does it come up onto the sidewalk?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:55:53-05:00",
      "duration": 28,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both. It spreads across the bottom of the sidewalk where people have to step to get around the snowbank. [pause] And there are kids that walk right through there to the bus. And the dog walkers, there are a lot of them on this street, early, when it's still dark. Somebody's going to go down hard. I'd rather not be the building that's on the news for it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:56:21-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I understand. Let me get this down so a crew can look at the drain. It sounds like it could be clogged or frozen over, one or the other."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:56:34-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Probably both. Sorry, hang on a second. [pause] Okay. I just chipped my favorite mug on the counter. Of course I did. Anyway. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:56:45-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh no, not the favorite. Sorry about that. Okay, so I have 179 Kingston Avenue, drain at the curb not draining, ponding and freezing overnight. Is the drain itself visible, or buried under snow?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:56:59-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Half buried. You can see the grate on one side. There's ice packed around it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:57:06-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that helps. I'll put that in the notes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:57:11-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So, will there actually be a work order opened? I'd like to know that, and for what date. Not just that it's been noted."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:57:21-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I'm opening a work order right now while we're talking. As for the date, I can tell you it goes to the drainage crew, and they're usually working through these within a few business days. So I'd say early next week is realistic, maybe Monday or Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:57:41-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Monday or Tuesday. Okay. And if somebody falls before then?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:57:46-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If it gets worse or it's an emergency, call us back right away and I'll flag it. Meanwhile keep salting or sanding it, that's the best thing you can do. Do you want a call back when the order's assigned?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:58:03-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. It's 401-555-0170."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:58:06-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "555-0170, got it. And that's the cell?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:58:10-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's the cell. It's the only one I answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:58:14-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. You'll get a call from us once it's scheduled. Anything else down there I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:58:22-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's it. Just the one puddle that has become a skating rink. Thank you, Denise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:58:29-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Ms. Tran. Stay off the ice, and good luck with the mug."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T10:58:35-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's survived worse. Bye now."
    }
  ],
